url: "https://velumspiritus.github.io/Meeting-Architecture/"
abstract: >-
  A 30-section brief with mathematical proof that boundaries are not the
  edge of a system — the boundary IS the system. Three independent
  substrates satisfy the axioms: a quartz crystal circuit (photographed
  oscilloscope evidence), observational density probes (4,503-row pulsar
  catalog), and the institutional record (76 names, 15 meetings, 41 events
  across 9 sectors). Includes the F operator, the torus FFT (254 lines,
  pure PyTorch, CUDA-native runnable proof of irrational winding on
  T² = S¹ × S¹), Fisher geodesic coupling, topology tournament,
  circuit schematics, and a 206-page Statement of Facts. 22 peer-reviewed
  citations across biology, physics, and mycology. All code runs.
keywords:
  - boundary function
  - compression theorem
  - torus FFT
  - winding numbers
  - coprime closure
  - crystal circuit
  - piezoelectric
  - F operator
  - institutional analysis
  - singularity resolution
